      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.104,
            0.116,
            0.118
          ],
          "content": "8"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.139,
            0.628,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, a and b have at least 3 as a common factor."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.165,
            0.615,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": "But this contradicts the fact that a and b are coprime."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.196,
            0.899,
            0.244
          ],
          "content": "This contradiction has arisen because of our incorrect assumption that $\\sqrt { 3 }$ is rational. So, we conclude that $\\sqrt { 3 }$ is irrational."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.252,
            0.462,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": "In Class IX, we mentioned that :"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.285,
            0.897,
            0.305
          ],
          "content": "the sum or difference of a rational and an irrational number is irrational and"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.319,
            0.901,
            0.356
          ],
          "content": "the product and quotient of a non-zero rational and irrational number is irrational."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.365,
            0.532,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": "We prove some particular cases here."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.395,
            0.528,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": "**Example 6 :** Show that $5 - { \\sqrt { 3 } }$ is irrational."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.427,
            0.728,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** Let us assume, to the contrary, that $5 \\sim \\sqrt { 3 }$ is rational."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.461,
            0.742,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": "That is, we can find coprime a and $b ( \\underline { b } \\neq 0 )$ such that $\\sqrt{3} = \\frac{a}{b}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.495,
            0.328,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, $5 - { \\frac { a } { b } } = { \\sqrt { 3 } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.531,
            0.638,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": "Rearranging this equation, we get $\\sqrt{3}=5-\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{5b-a}{b}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.572,
            0.814,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "Since a and b are integers, we get $5 - \\frac{a}{b}$ is rational, and so $\\sqrt { 3 }$ is rational."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.607,
            0.57,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": "But this contradicts the fact that $\\sqrt { 3 }$ is irrational."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.634,
            0.9,
            0.679
          ],
          "content": "This contradiction has arisen because of our incorrect assumption that $5 - \\sqrt { 3 }$ is rational."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.697,
            0.498,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": "So, we conclude that $5 \\geq \\sqrt { 3 }$ is irrational."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.738,
            0.504,
            0.758
          ],
          "content": "**Example 7 :** Show that $3 \\sqrt { 2 }$ is irrational."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.766,
            0.704,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** Let us assume, to the contrary, that $3 \\sqrt { 2 }$ is rational."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.797,
            0.718,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": "That is, we can find coprime a and $b \\; ( b \\neq 0 )$ such that $3 { \\sqrt { 2 } } = { \\frac { a } { b } } \\cdot$"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.967,
            0.563,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.831,
            0.397,
            0.866
          ],
          "content": "Rearranging, we get ${ \\sqrt { 2 } } = { \\frac { a } { 3 b } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.869,
            0.739,
            0.905
          ],
          "content": "Since 3, a and b are integers, $\\frac { a } { 3 b }$ is rational, and so $\\sqrt { 2 }$ is rational."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
